{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1634","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Fibonacci Additions"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of my most productive days was throwing away 1,000 lines of code."}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— Ken Thompson"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fibonacci addition"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an operation on an array $$$X$$$ of integers, parametrized by indices $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$. Fibonacci addition increases $$$X_l$$$ by $$$F_1$$$, increases $$$X_{l + 1}$$$ by $$$F_2$$$, and so on up to $$$X_r$$$ which is increased by $$$F_{r - l + 1}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$F_i$$$ denotes the $$$i$$$-th Fibonacci number ($$$F_1 = 1$$$, $$$F_2 = 1$$$, $$$F_{i} = F_{i - 1} + F_{i - 2}$$$ for $$$i \\gt 2$$$), and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all operations are performed modulo $$$MOD$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two arrays $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$ of the same length. We will ask you to perform several Fibonacci additions on these arrays with different parameters, and after each operation you have to report whether arrays $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$ are equal modulo $$$MOD$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains 3 numbers $$$n$$$, $$$q$$$ and $$$MOD$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, q \\le 3\\cdot 10^5, 1 \\le MOD \\le 10^9+7$$$) — the length of the arrays, the number of operations, and the number modulo which all operations are performed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ numbers — array $$$A$$$ ($$$0 \\le A_i \\lt MOD$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line also contains $$$n$$$ numbers — array $$$B$$$ ($$$0 \\le B_i \\lt MOD$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$q$$$ lines contain character $$$c$$$ and two numbers $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$ ($$$1 \\le l \\le r \\le n$$$) — operation parameters. If $$$c$$$ is \"A\", Fibonacci addition is to be performed on array $$$A$$$, and if it is is \"B\", the operation is to be performed on $$$B$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After each operation, print \"YES\" (without quotes) if the arrays are equal and \"NO\" otherwise. Letter case does not matter."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 5 3\n2 2 1\n0 0 0\nA 1 3\nA 1 3\nB 1 1\nB 2 2\nA 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nNO\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 3 10\n2 5 0 3 5\n3 5 8 2 5\nB 2 3\nB 3 4\nA 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation of the test from the condition:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Initially $$$A=[2,2,1]$$$, $$$B=[0,0,0]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After operation \"A 1 3\": $$$A=[0,0,0]$$$, $$$B=[0,0,0]$$$ (addition is modulo 3)."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After operation \"A 1 3\": $$$A=[1,1,2]$$$, $$$B=[0,0,0]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After operation \"B 1 1\": $$$A=[1,1,2]$$$, $$$B=[1,0,0]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After operation \"B 2 2\": $$$A=[1,1,2]$$$, $$$B=[1,1,0]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After operation \"A 3 3\": $$$A=[1,1,0]$$$, $$$B=[1,1,0]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1634F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1634/problem/F"}